@startuml observability-usage
title warren/observability — OTel wiring, span across the broker\nsource: warren.md §7.1, §3.4 (spec retired — the code, its tests and the manifest are the contract)

participant "main.go" as main
participant "observability.Module" as obs
participant "publishing side\n(handler → outbox → relay)" as producer
participant "Message.Headers" as headers
participant "consumer chain\n(TraceExtract stage)" as consumer

main -> obs : Module(\n  ServiceName("user-service"),\n  OTLPEndpoint(cfg.OTel.Endpoint),\n  SampleRatio(0.1))
note right : inert module; SDK wiring happens\nwhen the bootstrapper materialises\nthe graph — one import instruments\nHTTP, gRPC, consumers, DB, handlers

obs -> producer : span per handler,\nnamed <module>.<handler>
note right : handler instrumentation mechanism\nis the app carve-out (OQ 1)
producer -> headers : inject trace context\n(§3.4 reserves Headers for this)
headers -> consumer : ...through Kafka/AMQP/NATS...
consumer -> consumer : TraceExtract — consumer span\ncontinues the producer's trace
note right : "a span survives the trip\nthrough Kafka into the consumer"

note over obs : wraps SETUP, not the API —\ntrace.Tracer stays directly accessible
@enduml
